<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan raw sugar imports up 28.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan raw sugar imports up 28.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's raw sugar imports in January totalled 112,212 tonnes, up 28.3 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			   Jan 97	Dec 96	   Jan 96</p>
<p> Total		  112,212     134,281	  87,443</p>
<p>Main suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand		35,274	10,342	  10,009</p>
<p> South Africa	  23,447	   nil	     nil</p>
<p> Australia	     53,491     100,966	  77,434</p>
<p> Fiji			 nil	22,953	     nil</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in 1996 totalled 1,651,086 tonnes, down 4.6 percent from 1,730,506 tonnes during the prior year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
